# --- App ---
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:4321
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:5173
# Post-report guide: three lines for each person before they walk into the
# conversation - a way to open, a question to carry, and one thing the other person
# said worth taking seriously.
#
# This comment used to say "not yet rendered by any UI. OFF by default so it does not
# spend a Gemini call per participant per release into a void" - and the flag was set
# to true underneath it. So the call was spent every release, for every person, and
# the result was discarded. Found by diffing what the report returns against what the
# client reads; the comment had predicted the exact failure.
#
# The surface exists now: "Before you talk to them" on the report, shown only to the
# person whose guide it is. On is the right setting, and the default when unset (22 November 2026).
POST_REPORT_GUIDE_ENABLED=true

# The confidence read: what the lead can weigh, and where the picture is thin.
#
# On, as of wave 14. It was written off by default because what sits behind it are
# sentences a person reads about their own record, and if that landed wrong the fix
# had to be one variable rather than a revert with reports already sent.
#
# Turned on after checking the arithmetic against a real closed twelve-session
# ground rather than a fixture. Both parties came back with no soft spots, which is
# the correct answer there - each corroborates the other, the detail moves session
# to session, and the one attached document is actually referred to. Each of the
# three spots was then shown to fire on a shape that deserves it, and the false
# positive Hafsah caught twice - a lead whose account is all targets nobody else
# could corroborate - correctly stays silent.
#
# On unless set to exactly "false" (22 November 2026: nothing is switched off by default).
CONFIDENCE_ENABLED=true

# --- Database (PostgreSQL) ---
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/groundwork?schema=public"

# --- JWT ---
JWT_SECRET=change-me-in-production
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d

# --- Anthropic (conversation engine, report synthesis, pattern detection) ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
# Gemini: GEMINI_MODEL writes reports and synthesis; GEMINI_CONVERSATION_MODEL is what a person talks to
# in Setup and check-ins (fast, no thinking). Both default in configuration.ts.
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro
GEMINI_CONVERSATION_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
ANTHROPIC_MAX_TOKENS=2048

# --- Billing gate ---
# Set to "true" in production to enforce Stripe payment before activating grounds.
# Leave unset (or "false") in development to skip the payment wall.
BILLING_ENABLED=false

# --- Stripe (USD billing) ---
# Subscription prices are NOT set here - they live in the pricing_plans table,
# edited at Admin -> System -> Pricing. These three are the only Stripe env
# vars the app reads; STRIPE_CALLBACK_URL should point at the deployed client
# origin (not localhost) in any shared environment.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
STRIPE_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:5173/billing/callback

# --- Resend (transactional email) ---
# REQUIRED: get your key from https://resend.com/api-keys
# Without a real key ALL emails (invites, password reset, magic links) are suppressed.
# The placeholder re_... is detected and falls back to console-only logging.
# EMAIL. Both of these are checked at boot IN PRODUCTION and the API refuses to
# start without them (see assertProductionConfig in src/main.ts). A placeholder
# key counts as missing: "re_..." and "re_test" are both rejected on purpose,
# because a deployment that boots and silently posts nothing is worse than one
# that will not boot.
EMAIL_SENDS_FOR_REAL=false
# Leave empty rather than writing a placeholder here. "re_..." and "re_test" are
# both rejected by name at boot, so an example carrying one hands somebody a
# value that cannot work.
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL="Groundwork <noreply@myground.work>"
# Signs the Resend webhook (Svix scheme). Without it the endpoint FAILS CLOSED and rejects
# everything - which means no delivery tracking AND no inbound mail, since both arrive there.
RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# Mail sent TO us. hello@myground.work is on the marketing site; point a Resend inbound route at
# POST /webhooks/resend and it appears at Platform ops -> Inbox. Until then it only reaches
# whoever owns the mailbox.

# --- Google OAuth (optional) ---
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/google/callback

# Meta signs inbound WhatsApp webhooks with this. WITHOUT IT THE INBOUND PATH IS DEAD BY DESIGN:
# verification fails closed, so an unconfigured deployment cannot be sent forged messages.
# Distinct from WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN, which only answers Meta's subscribe handshake.
WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET=

# --- Platform admin (the back office) ---
# The one-time bootstrap for the FIRST platform admin. It promotes a person who has ALREADY signed
# up through the normal flow - it never creates an account, because inventing a user with no
# password and no verified address would be a worse answer than saying so.
#
# It is a no-op unless BOTH are true: this is set, and no platform admin exists anywhere yet. Once
# one exists it never fires again, so it cannot add a second admin or re-promote somebody who was
# demoted. Everyone after the first goes through POST /admin/add-admin, which needs an existing
# platform admin and an OTP.
#
# Undocumented here until now, and that omission has a cost on record: an operator set nothing on a
# fresh install, got no admin and no error, and the back-office review surfaces were unreachable for
# an entire eighteen-ground test run. The conclusion drawn at the time was that the feature did not
# exist. GW-002.
#
# Order that works: sign the address up, set this, restart the API, watch for the
# "promoted ... to platform admin" line at WARN.
PLATFORM_ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_EMAIL=

# The Vertex service account, as one line of JSON. Also checked at boot in
# production; the API refuses to start without it.
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
